<title>USA: USDA gross cutout hide and offal value.</title>
<headline>USDA gross cutout hide and offal value.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The hide and offal value from a typical slaughter steer for today was estimated at $9.66 per cwt live, up 0.03 when compared to Thursday's value.-USDA</p>
<p>FOB CENTRAL U.S., TODAY'S CALCULATIONS FOR BY-PRODUCT VALUE</p>
<p>(STEER) -			  Lbs    Price  Change    Value</p>
<p>Steer hide, butt brand	 5.33   89.00    0.50    6.08</p>
<p>Tallow, edible		   1.20   23.75    -	 0.29</p>
<p>Tallow, packer bleachable    4.50   18.25    -	 0.82</p>
<p>Tongues, Swiss #1 Wht 0-3%   0.26  180.00    -	 0.47</p>
<p>Cheek meat, trmd		 0.32   72.75    -	 0.23</p>
<p>Head meat			  0.13   56.50    -	 0.07</p>
<p>Oxtail, selected		 0.16  151.00    -	 0.24</p>
<p>Hearts, reg, bone out	  0.38   31.00    -	 0.12</p>
<p>Lips, unscalded		  0.11   72.00    -	 0.08</p>
<p>Livers, slcted, gall off     0.96   38.00    -	 0.36</p>
<p>Tripe, scalded edible	  0.65   20.00    -	 0.13</p>
<p>Tripe, honeycomb bleached    0.15   41.00    -	 0.06</p>
<p>Lungs, inedible		  0.47    4.60    -	 0.02</p>
<p>Melts				0.14    6.25    -	 0.01</p>
<p>Meat bone ml, 50% blk/ton    3.70  280.00    0.50    0.52</p>
<p>Blood meal, 85% blk/ton	0.60  525.00    -	 0.16</p>
<p>TOTAL :			   19.06			  9.66</p>
<p>The average value of hide and offal for the five days ending Friday, March 7, 1997 was estimated at 9.62 per cwt., down -0.02 from last week and up 1.61 from last year.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
